---
---

<section class="language-model" aria-labelledby="language-model-title">
	<p class="label">One rule</p>
	<h2 id="language-model-title">Indentation becomes structure.</h2>
	<p class="lede">
		CCL keeps the file readable while giving implementers one predictable rule:
		each indented line belongs to the nearest parent above it. The same source
		resolves the same way for people, parsers, and AI tools.
	</p>
	<p class="rule">
		<code>parent = nearest less-indented row</code>
		<span>No block markers, no delimiters &mdash; the layout is the hierarchy.</span>
	</p>
</section>

<style>
	.language-model {
		padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8.5rem) 0;
	}

	.label {
		display: inline-block;
		margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
		padding: 0.28rem 0.8rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ccl-contrast) 20%, transparent);
		border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ccl-contrast) 40%, transparent);
		color: var(--ccl-contrast-high);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 18ch;
		font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.7rem);
		line-height: 1.02;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.lede {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		max-width: 54ch;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		line-height: 1.65;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.rule {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		max-width: 32rem;
		margin: 2rem 0 0;
		padding: 1.1rem 0;
		border-block: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ccl-contrast) 38%, transparent);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.rule code {
		color: var(--ccl-contrast-high);
		font-family: "Fira Code", ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.rule span {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
</style>
